2026-09-27T09:10:27.6841766Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6842113Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6842433Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6843179Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6844041Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6844122Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6844308Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6844604Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6844870Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6844957Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6845176Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6845556Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6845722Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6846084Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6846297Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6846408Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6846676Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6846849Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6846982Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6847364Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6847741Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6848400Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6848927Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6849171Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6849593Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6850121Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6850400Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6850692Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6851090Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6851170Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6851357Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6851466Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6852875Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6854199Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6854412Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6921662Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6922809Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6923456Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6924032Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6924492Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6924907Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6925017Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6925490Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6925759Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6926825Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6927988Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6928634Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6929499Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:27.6929712Z 
